Q: How to remove leading zeros from a string A: <p>You could on optional leading zeroes</p>
<pre><code>$str = preg_split(&quot;/^0*/&quot;, &quot;0044800 999999&quot;, 2);
var_dump($str[1]);
</code></pre>
<p>Output</p>
<pre><code>string(12) &quot;44800 999999&quot;
</code></pre>
<p>Or you could split on 1 or more leading zeroes, and check if the returned array has 2 parts in case the string did not contain leading zeroes.</p>
<hr>
<p>You might use a more precise approach removing leading zeroes, and use a capture group to match digits followed by a space and digits.</p>
<pre><code>$re = '/^0*(\d+(?:\h+\d+)*)$/';
$str = '0044800 999999';
$result = preg_replace($re, '$1', $str);
var_dump($result);
</code></pre>
<p>Output</p>
<pre><code>string(12) &quot;44800 999999&quot;
</code></pre>

